public with sharing class PicklistService {

    public class PicklistServiceException extends Exception {}

    public class Option {
        public String value;
        public String label;
        public Boolean isDefault;
    }

    public static List<Option> activeOptions(String objectApiName, String fieldApiName) {
        if (objectApiName == null || fieldApiName == null
            || objectApiName.trim() == '' || fieldApiName.trim() == '') {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Object and field API names must not be null or blank.');
        }

        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objDescribe = getObjectDescribe(objectApiName);
        Schema.DescribeFieldResult fldDescribe = getFieldDescribe(objDescribe, fieldApiName);

        if (fldDescribe.getType() != Schema.DisplayType.PICKLIST
            && fldDescribe.getType() != Schema.DisplayType.MULTISELECTLIST) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Field [' + fieldApiName + '] on [' + objectApiName + '] is not a picklist or multi-select picklist; actual type: '
                + fldDescribe.getType());
        }

        String defaultValue = fldDescribe.getDefaultValue();

        List<Option> options = new List<Option>();
        for (Schema.PicklistEntry pe : fldDescribe.getPicklistValues()) {
            if (!pe.isActive()) {
                continue;
            }
            Option opt = new Option();
            opt.value = pe.getValue();
            opt.label = pe.getLabel();
            opt.isDefault = defaultValue != null && pe.getValue() == defaultValue;
            options.add(opt);
        }
        return options;
    }

    private static Schema.DescribeSObjectResult getObjectDescribe(String objectApiName) {
        Map<String, Schema.SObjectType> globalMap = Schema.getGlobalDescribe();
        String target = objectApiName.toLowerCase();
        for (String key : globalMap.keySet()) {
            if (key.toLowerCase() == target) {
                return globalMap.get(key).getDescribe();
            }
        }
        throw new PicklistServiceException('Object does not exist: ' + objectApiName);
    }

    private static Schema.DescribeFieldResult getFieldDescribe(Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objDescribe, String fieldApiName) {
        Map<String, Schema.SObjectField> fieldMap = objDescribe.fields;
        String target = fieldApiName.toLowerCase();
        for (String key : fieldMap.keySet()) {
            if (key.toLowerCase() == target) {
                return fieldMap.get(key).getDescribe();
            }
        }
        throw new PicklistServiceException(
            'Field does not exist on object: ' + fieldApiName + ' (on ' + objDescribe.getName() + ')');
    }
}
```

**How it works:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| Null / blank input | Explicit null + trim check before any dereference → throws `PicklistServiceException` |
| Case-insensitive object | Iterates `Schema.getGlobalDescribe()` keys with a lowercase comparison |
| Case-insensitive field | Iterates the object's `fields` map the same way |
| Object not found | `getObjectDescribe` throws `PicklistServiceException` |
| Field not found | `getFieldDescribe` throws `PicklistServiceException` |
| Wrong field type | Checks `DisplayType.PICKLIST` / `MULTISELECTLIST`; anything else throws |
| Inactive values | Filtered out with `pe.isActive()` |
| Order | `getPicklistValues()` already returns values in the order defined on the field |
| Default value | Compared via `fldDescribe.getDefaultValue()`; `isDefault` is `true` only for that one entry |
| No NPE / other exceptions | Every path that could fail throws the custom exception before any unsafe dereference |

