## Analysis

The requirements map directly to the **Composite API** (`/composite`) with `allOrNone: false`:

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| One API call for both orders | Single `POST /composite` with all four sub-requests in the body |
| One unit of work per order, independent | `allOrNone: false` – each sub-request commits/rolls back on its own |
| A failing order never blocks others | Same – independent transactions per sub-request |
| All-or-nothing per order | The Opportunity references the Account via `@referenceId`; if the upsert fails the reference is unresolvable and the Opportunity fails too, so the order is not partially saved |
