public class HouseholdService {

    /**
     * Creates a single NPSP Household Account for the given contacts.
     * The first contact becomes the household's primary contact (npe01__One2OneContact__c).
     * All contacts are assigned to that one household.
     *
     * @param members  New Contact objects (no Id, no AccountId). Must not be null or empty.
     * @return The Id of the newly created Household Account.
     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if members is null or empty.
     */
    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must not be null or empty');
        }

        // 1. Insert the contacts without an AccountId so no extra households are created.
        insert members;

        // 2. Look up the Household RecordType by DeveloperName (avoids hard-coded Ids).
        RecordType hhRt = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM RecordType
            WHERE SObjectType = 'Account'
              AND DeveloperName = 'HH_Account'
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        // 3. Create the household Account.
        //    Do NOT set Name – NPSP will auto-name it when contacts are assigned.
        //    Point One2OneContact__c at the first member so NPSP knows the primary contact.
        Account household = new Account(
            RecordTypeId = hhRt.Id,
            npe01__One2OneContact__c = members[0].Id
        );
        insert household;

        // 4. Assign every contact to the household.
        for (Contact c : members) {
            c.AccountId = household.Id;
        }
        update members;

        return household.Id;
    }
}
```

**How it satisfies each requirement:**

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| One household for all contacts | A single `Account` is created; every contact is updated with that account's Id. |
| First contact = primary | `npe01__One2OneContact__c` is set to `members[0].Id` at insert time. |
| Real NPSP household | `RecordTypeId` is resolved at runtime from `DeveloperName = 'HH_Account'`, so NPSP's trigger names the household and generates greetings. |
| No hard-coded RT Ids | The Id is fetched via a SOQL on `RecordType`. |
| No name set manually | `Account.Name` is left null; NPSP's naming trigger handles it when contacts are linked. |
| No orphan/extra accounts | Contacts are first inserted *without* an `AccountId` (standalone, no household created), then assigned to the one household we create. |
| Guard clause | `IllegalArgumentException` thrown for null or empty list. |

