```apex
public with sharing class AccountOwnershipService {

    /**
     * Reassigns the given Accounts and all their Contacts to a new owner.
     *
     * Account trigger actions are bypassed for the duration of the Account DML
     * (territory recalculation, etc.) and cleared in a finally block so that
     * Account automation resumes normally for the remainder of the transaction.
     * Contact trigger actions run normally.
     *
     * Bulk-safe: uses at most 2 SOQL queries and 2 DML statements regardless of volume.
     * All-or-none: exceptions propagate to the caller; the caller (or an outer
     * transaction boundary) is responsible for rollback.
     *
     * @param accountIds  Up to 200 Account IDs to reassign.
     * @param newOwnerId  The User Id of the new owner.
     */
    public static void reassign(Set<Id> accountIds, Id newOwnerId) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // SOQL 1 – load the target Accounts
        List<Account> accounts = [SELECT Id FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds];

        // SOQL 2 – load all Contacts belonging to those Accounts
        List<Contact> contacts = [SELECT Id FROM Contact WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds];

        // Set the new owner on Accounts
        for (Account acc : accounts) {
            acc.OwnerId = newOwnerId;
        }

        // Set the new owner on Contacts
        for (Contact con : contacts) {
            con.OwnerId = newOwnerId;
        }

        // Bypass ALL Account trigger actions for this DML only.
        // Contact actions are unaffected and will execute normally.
        TriggerBase.bypass('Account');
        try {
            // DML 1 – update Accounts (trigger actions suppressed)
            update accounts;

            // DML 2 – update Contacts (trigger actions run normally)
            update contacts;
        }
        finally {
            // Guarantee Account automation is restored regardless of outcome
            TriggerBase.clearBypass('Account');
        }
    }
}
```

**Design rationale:**

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| Account trigger actions suppressed | `TriggerBase.bypass('Account')` before the Account DML |
| Contact actions run normally | No bypass is placed on `Contact`; only `Account` is bypassed |
| Automation restored after `reassign` | `TriggerBase.clearBypass('Account')` in a `finally` block executes on both success and failure paths |
| All-or-none, exceptions propagate | No `try/catch` that swallows; the `finally` only cleans up the bypass—any exception bubbles to the caller unchanged |
| ≤ 2 SOQL queries | One query for Accounts, one for Contacts (both keyed on the passed `accountIds`) |
| ≤ 2 DML statements | One `update accounts`, one `update contacts` |
| Bulk-safe to 200 | Collection-based DML; no per-record governor spikes |
| Security | `with sharing` enforces the caller's access to both the Accounts and their Contacts |

