**How it works end-to-end:**

| Scenario | 1st trigger (user DML) | 2nd trigger (rounding DML) | Tasks created |
|---|---|---|---|
| Amount 100 → 100.55 (needs rounding to 101) | count=1, amount changed → Task | count=2 → skip | **1** |
| Amount 100 → 200 (already whole) | count=1, amount changed → Task | no 2nd trigger for this record | **1** |
| Amount unchanged (other field edited) | count=1, amount same → no Task | no 2nd trigger | **0** |

The single `insert tasksToInsert` call keeps us well within governor limits for 200 opportunities (1 DML statement for up to 200 Tasks, plus the framework's own bookkeeping).

